ARTICLE 8.61-W
Cooperation
1. The Parties shall, as appropriate, cooperate and participate actively in
international fora, including the WTO, to promote the development of
international frameworks for digital trade.
2. The Parties shall endeavour to:
(a) exchange information and share experiences  and best practices  on
regulatory matters relating to the digital economy, including:
(i) personal information protection;
(ii) data governance;
(iii) cross-border data flows;
(iv) online consumer protection, including means for consumer
redress and building consumer confidence;
(v) unsolicited commercial electronic messages;
(vi) electronic contracts;
(vii) electronic trust and electronic authentication services;
(viii) digital identities;

